-- Threshold-pressure smoke test: DUMPFLUX producer.
--
-- Two equilibration regions split at i=5/6, so the region boundary runs the
-- full depth of the grid. The initial pressure jump across it grows with
-- depth, from 1 bar in the top layer to 10 bar in the bottom one, which makes
-- the defaulted THPRES entry between the regions about 10 bar.
--
-- The sector selected below covers only the top three layers, so a reduced run
-- left to work the threshold out for itself sees a jump of at most 3 bar and
-- arrives at roughly a third of the right answer. That is the whole point of
-- the test: the number cannot be recomputed from a sector, only carried.

RUNSPEC

WATER
GAS
OIL

METRIC

UNIFOUT

DIMENS
  10 1 10 /

TABDIMS
  1 1 40 20 1 20 /

EQLDIMS
  2 /

EQLOPTS
  'THPRES' /

GRID

DX
  100*1 /
DY
  100*1 /
DZ
  100*1 /

TOPS
  10*0. /

PORO
  100*0.3 /

PERMX
  100*500 /

-- The sector: i = 4..7 of the top three layers, straddling the region
-- boundary at i=5/6 but holding only three of its ten faces.
FLUXNUM
  3*0 4*1 3*0
  3*0 4*1 3*0
  3*0 4*1 3*0
  70*0 /

FLUXTYPE
  PRESSURE /

DUMPFLUX /

INIT

